CloudBurrow patch 14 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1340). Needs googlesqlite patch 0027.

The bug: a table made by tables.insert with a column's
defaultValueExpression kept the expression in its metadata, but the
engine's table was made without a DEFAULT (contentdata's CreateTable), so
`INSERT INTO t (id) VALUES (1)` read the column back NULL; and
tabledata.insertAll, the Storage Write API and loads (AddTableData) gave
every column of every row, NULL for one a row left out, so no default was
ever applied. A table made by CREATE TABLE ... DEFAULT had its default in
the engine, but tables.get had no defaultValueExpression for the column
(addTableMetadata). Measured through CloudBurrow's front, 2026-10-15.

BigQuery keeps the expression in the schema and applies it to an insert
that leaves the column out; "NULL values in the loaded data are not
converted to default values" (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/default-values).
The patch makes a top-level column's defaultValueExpression its DEFAULT
in the engine; leaves a column with a default out of the INSERT of a row
that does not give it (a NULL given stays NULL), consecutive rows that
give the same columns by one statement, in their order; and gives a
CREATE TABLE column its DEFAULT's text as its defaultValueExpression.
server/column_defaults_test.go fails without the patch and passes with
it.

